    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald are delighted to present No. 9 The Pines, a spacious and well-maintained four-bedroom semi-detached family home, ideally located in a quiet and mature residential setting in the heart of Killester.\n\nThis attractive property offers a wonderful balance of living and bedroom accommodation, complemented by a private rear garden and the added benefit of a versatile outdoor studio—ideal for use as a home office, gym, or creative space.\n\nUpon entering, the home opens into a welcoming hallway leading to a bright and comfortable living room to the front. To the rear, there is a well-appointed kitchen with ample storage and workspace, overlooking the garden and filled with natural light. The layout is practical and suited to modern family living.\n\nUpstairs, the accommodation comprises four well-proportioned bedrooms along with a family bathroom, offering flexibility for growing families or those working from home.\n\nExternally, the rear garden provides a private outdoor retreat with a mix of patio and lawn space, while the standalone studio adds valuable additional accommodation. To the front, there is off-street parking and a neatly maintained approach.\n\nThe location is second to none, with Killester Village, excellent schools, parks, and a range of amenities all within easy reach. The area is very well serviced by public transport, including the DART, and offers convenient access to Dublin city centre, the M1, M50, and Dublin Airport.\n\nThis is an excellent opportunity to acquire a turnkey family home with additional flexible space in a highly sought-after location."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 5.5m x 1.7m\nWelcoming entrance hall with varnished wooden flooring.\n\nKitchen - 5.7m x 3.4m\nShaker style fitted double fronted kitchen with quality integrated appliances and ample storage space.\n\nLiving Room - 5.3m x 3.4m\nWooden flooring with feature fireplace and sliding door to rear garden space.\n\nBathroom - 2.6m x 2.8m\nWash hand basin, toilet and sink\n\nStudio - 2.7m x 2.7m\nWired and heated.\n\nLanding - 3.1m x 2.7m\nCarpeted flooring with attic access.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.3m x 3.1m\nWooden flooring with fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.2m x 3.2m\nWooden flooring.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.1m x 2.0m\nWooden flooring with fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.3m x 2.1m\nWooden flooring.\n\nBathroom - 2.2m x 2.0m\nWith electric shower, bath, toilet and sink.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Spacious four-bedroom end-of-terrace family home </li><li> Well-maintained and presented in good condition throughout </li><li> Four well-sized bedrooms </li><li> Family bathroom </li><li> Private rear garden with patio and lawn space </li><li> Detached outdoor studio ideal for home office, gym, or additional storage </li><li> Side access enhancing practicality </li><li> Off-street parking to the front </li><li> Quiet cul-de-sac setting within a mature development </li><li> Highly sought-after Killester location </li><li> Close to shops, cafés, schools, and local amenities </li><li> Walking distance to Killester DART station </li><li> Excellent transport links to Dublin city centre </li><li> Easy access to M1, M50, and Dublin Airport</ul>"
      },
